From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 20:23:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(gastown): pass --include-infra on every wisp
 reconciliation lookup
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Wisps are infrastructure beads, which `gc bd list` hides by default. Every
wisp-reconciliation snippet in the gastown pack was built on a bare
`gc bd list ... --type=molecule`, so it returned `[]` even when open wisps
existed and were assigned to the agent.

The agent therefore concluded "no wisp queued" on every restart, poured a
fresh wisp, and leaked the predecessor. The surplus-burn loops in the same
recipes could never self-correct, because the list they iterate is always
empty — so wisp growth is unbounded. This is the #1884 wisp-leak failure
mode, reachable straight from the documented recipe.

The role templates contradicted themselves: the generic startup-check
snippet is rendered by the gc binary and is ephemeral/infra-aware, while
these role-specific snippets hardcoded in the pack were not.

Fixed at 14 lookup sites (plus one prose reference to a closed-wisp query):

  agents/witness/prompt.template.md    Startup Protocol step 1 (x2),
                                       No Idle State fallback (x2)
  agents/deacon/prompt.template.md     CURRENT_WISP, ASSIGNED_WISP
  agents/refinery/prompt.template.md   CURRENT_WISP (x2)
  formulas/mol-witness-patrol.toml     next-iteration OPEN_WISPS
  formulas/mol-deacon-patrol.toml      next-iteration CURRENT_WISP
  formulas/mol-refinery-patrol.toml    CURRENT_WISP (x5) + prose

Also documents why the flag is load-bearing at each site, so the next
editor does not drop it.

Verified against bd 1.1.0 on a live city — the blind form returns [] while
the fixed form surfaces the leaked wisps on both the town and rig ledgers:

  $ gc bd list --assignee=gastown.deacon --status=open --type=molecule --limit=0 --json
  []
  $ gc bd list --assignee=gastown.deacon --status=open --type=molecule --include-infra --limit=0 --json
  gc-wisp-2ruzaj  open  molecule  gastown.deacon
  gc-wisp-1358ts  open  molecule  gastown.deacon

Note: `bd list --include-ephemeral` does not exist (unknown flag on bd
1.1.0); `--include-infra` is the correct flag.

Downstream: gascity's examples/gastown/gastown_test.go asserts two of these
snippets as exact full-line strings (gastown_test.go:2881-2882) and will
need updating when gascity bumps its gascity-packs dependency. The prefix
assertions at :2328-2341 are unaffected.

